WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.055 --> 00:00:08.515
The ghost beckoned for Scrooge to continue through the town and walk along a narrow lane.

2
00:00:08.516 --> 00:00:14.316
After a while they approached a large, red-brick building with a belltower.

3
00:00:14.317 --> 00:00:17.230
Scrooge felt a chill when he saw it.

4
00:00:17.231 --> 00:00:20.742
The building had once been a fine mansion.

5
00:00:20.743 --> 00:00:29.706
But it had fallen on hard times since then, with mossy walls and broken windows.

6
00:00:29.707 --> 00:00:36.394
"I see that you remember your old boarding school," the ghost said.

7
00:00:36.395 --> 00:00:41.658
"It's nearly Christmas Day, but it's not quite deserted.

8
00:00:41.659 --> 00:00:50.604
There's still one child there, a solitary boy neglected by his friends and family."

9
00:00:50.605 --> 00:00:56.661
"I know." Scrooge choked back a sob.

10
00:00:56.662 --> 00:01:00.805
He knew exactly which boy had been left alone at school.

11
00:01:00.806 --> 00:01:08.166
He wanted to turn away from the building, but the spirit pulled him inside.

12
00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:11.337
They entered a room at the back of the school.

13
00:01:11.338 --> 00:01:16.610
Inside, Scrooge saw himself as a boy, sitting at a desk.

14
00:01:16.611 --> 00:01:21.141
The boy was just a year or two older than the one who had built the snowman.

15
00:01:21.142 --> 00:01:25.694
He was all alone with only his books for company.

16
00:01:25.695 --> 00:01:30.465
Tears streamed down Scrooge's face as he remembered the day.

17
00:01:30.466 --> 00:01:38.604
"My father wouldn't allow me to come home for the Christmas holiday," he whispered.

18
00:01:38.605 --> 00:01:42.678
"He said it would do me more good to stay here and study.

19
00:01:42.679 --> 00:01:47.103
He said nobody at home would miss me."

20
00:01:47.104 --> 00:01:53.573
"Now let's see another Christmas," the ghost said gently.

21
00:01:53.574 --> 00:01:59.461
The young Ebenezer at the desk grew taller, turning into a young man.

22
00:01:59.462 --> 00:02:06.890
The school remained empty because once more, all the other students had gone home for Christmas.

23
00:02:06.891 --> 00:02:12.788
Young Ebenezer started pacing back and forth, occasionally glancing out the window.

24
00:02:12.789 --> 00:02:17.063
His face wore a look of despair and gloom.

25
00:02:17.064 --> 00:02:20.667
Then there was a noise outside the door.

26
00:02:20.668 --> 00:02:23.529
Young Ebenezer spun around to face it.

27
00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:29.799
The door flew open, and a girl with shiny curls and a happy face burst in.

28
00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:32.667
Scrooge recognized her at once.

29
00:02:32.668 --> 00:02:36.660
"It's my younger sister," he said with wonder.

30
00:02:36.661 --> 00:02:42.236
"My beloved little Fan. She looks just as I remember her."

31
00:02:42.237 --> 00:02:47.660
"Ebenezer!" The little girl flung herself at the young man.

32
00:02:47.661 --> 00:02:50.294
He caught her in a hug.

33
00:02:50.295 --> 00:02:55.374
"I have come to bring you home, my dear, dear brother!"

34
00:02:55.375 --> 00:03:01.587
Young Ebenezer gasped. "What? Home?"

35
00:03:01.588 --> 00:03:06.303
"Yes, home!" Fan said, laughing.

36
00:03:06.304 --> 00:03:09.940
"Home for good, forever and ever.

37
00:03:09.941 --> 00:03:13.399
Father is so much kinder than he used to be.

38
00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:20.413
He spoke so gently to me one day, I got the courage to ask him again to bring you home."

39
00:03:20.414 --> 00:03:25.272
"And he said yes?" Young Ebenezer sounded shocked.

40
00:03:25.273 --> 00:03:28.554
"Yes! He sent me in the coach to fetch you.

41
00:03:28.555 --> 00:03:34.568
And he said that since you're nearly a man now, there's no need to return to school ever again."

42
00:03:34.569 --> 00:03:42.511
Fan beamed. "We'll all be together for Christmas, and we'll have the merriest time in the world!"

43
00:03:42.512 --> 00:03:51.197
"Oh, Fan, I can't believe it," young Ebenezer said. "How wonderful."

44
00:03:51.198 --> 00:03:53.988
The ghost turned to Scrooge.

45
00:03:53.989 --> 00:03:57.864
"Your sister was always a delicate creature.

46
00:03:57.865 --> 00:04:04.208
A breath might have knocked her over. But she had a big heart."

47
00:04:04.209 --> 00:04:11.861
"So she did." Scrooge nodded. "I won't argue with you about that."

48
00:04:11.862 --> 00:04:18.398
"She lived long enough to have her own children, did she not?" the ghost asked.

49
00:04:18.399 --> 00:04:22.326
"One son," Scrooge said uneasily.

50
00:04:22.327 --> 00:04:30.910
He couldn't help thinking of Fred's visit earlier in the day— and how harshly he'd dismissed his nephew.

51
00:04:30.911 --> 00:04:36.569
The ghost touched Scrooge's heart, and now they stood in a busy section of London.

52
00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:44.421
It was Christmas Eve again, and the streetlights cast a warm glow over the cold scene.

53
00:04:44.422 --> 00:04:48.466
The ghost stopped in front of a warehouse.

54
00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:57.303
"I know where we are!" Scrooge said. "I was an apprentice here as a young man."

55
00:04:57.304 --> 00:05:00.849
He followed the ghost inside.

56
00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:06.517
An old gentleman in a wig sat at a very tall desk in the center of the room.

57
00:05:06.518 --> 00:05:10.745
Scrooge nearly laughed with delight as he gazed at the man.

58
00:05:10.746 --> 00:05:17.459
"Why, it's old Fezziwig! Bless his heart, it's Fezziwig alive again!"

59
00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:22.134
At that moment Mr. Fezziwig looked at the clock and laid down his pen.

60
00:05:22.135 --> 00:05:26.529
"Yo, ho, Ebenezer! Dick!" he called.

61
00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:30.979
Scrooge saw himself as a young man come hurrying into the room.

62
00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:36.959
He was followed by another young man, someone Scrooge hadn't seen in years.

63
00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:40.901
"That's Dick Wilkins," Scrooge said.

64
00:05:40.902 --> 00:05:45.539
"He was once quite impressed with me, as I recall."

65
00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:51.545
"No more work tonight, my boys," Fezziwig said, grinning at the two young men.

66
00:05:51.546 --> 00:06:01.883
"It's Christmas Eve. Let's clear space for our holiday party!"

